WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:04.140
hey all, it'sPprofessor Dave, I want to
continue talking about elimination reactions

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:05.920
specifically the E1 reaction.

00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:17.960
so the E1 reaction is to the E2 reaction
as the SN1 reaction is to the SN2 reaction

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:21.779
so basically as you'd expect, the E1
reaction is going to be

00:00:21.779 --> 00:00:25.170
two steps with a unimolecular transition state

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:29.750
just like with the SN1

00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:33.399
the first step in the E1 reaction is
that the leaving group leaves

00:00:33.399 --> 00:00:37.130
so let's take a look at this substrate
here the bromine is gonna leave

00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:42.300
that leaves a tertiary carbocation,
now it's very very important to understand

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:45.610
that while this substrate, this carbon is

00:00:45.610 --> 00:00:49.660
sp3 hybridized and therefore has
tetrahedral geometry

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:52.930
anytime a carbon that is sp3 hybridized

00:00:52.930 --> 00:00:56.800
loses an electron domain, because
this bromine is leaving

00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:01.510
with the electrons in that bond now this
carbon atom has only

00:01:01.510 --> 00:01:06.250
three electron domains and anything surrounded by three electron domains will

00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:11.460
exhibit trigonal planar geometry so it
is the case that this methyl group is now

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:15.229
flat in the board, this is now a flat
molecule with respect to the carbons

00:01:15.229 --> 00:01:18.490
so there is a formal positive charge now

00:01:18.490 --> 00:01:22.390
and so that means even a weak nucleophile like water can go ahead do an

00:01:22.390 --> 00:01:23.720
acid-base reaction

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:26.900
and grab that proton, so here is oxygen

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:30.079
interacting with this proton and then

00:01:30.079 --> 00:01:34.630
the electrons in this carbon-hydrogen
bond are the ones that go to form

00:01:34.630 --> 00:01:37.829
the carbon-carbon pi bond in the product

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:42.080
thanks for watching, guys. subscribe to my
channel for more tutorials

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:44.200
and as always feel free to email me with questions

